# The epilogue week at a safehouse (docs/EPILOGUE.md): the world's outcome, who was there and this
# player's route are kept apart. The first true variant is the greeting. {resident} is the house's
# own seeded name, never one from the lore.

conv epilogue.occupant.greet
for occupant
when epilogue
greet
prio reaction
voice haven

node start
  say? was:every_name :: "You were at the table when the names were read. I saw you. Sit down, there's soup. Real soup, with things in it. We're all leaving soon, and I wanted you to have a bowl first."
  say? cure_held:bastion :: "The cure came up the road in a crate with a number on it. We're on Bastion's list for it now. Everyone's on a list now. Mrs {resident} says at least it's a list with an end."
  say? cure_held:everyone :: "Somebody walked the cure out to every house. Ours came in a cold box at dawn. Mrs {resident} asked who to thank, and nobody would say. So we thank everybody, at supper."
  say? ending:every_name=every_name :: "They read every name at supper, even the crossed-out ones. Mrs {resident} cried, then went to bed early. We're leaving in a few days. The bear stays on the door."
  say? epilogue :: "The loudspeakers at the road checkpoints say processing now, not remain indoors. Nobody from {here} has gone up yet. Nobody quite believes it. We're packing slowly."

conv epilogue.occupant.route
for occupant
when epilogue & route:bastion
topic "I stood with Bastion, at the end."
prio reaction
once
voice haven

node start
  say "I know. Everyone in {here} knows. Bastion's crates came up the road with a number stencilled on every one, and now we're all on their list, in their order, when they say."
  say "Don't expect soup. There's soup. Don't expect it, that's all. Some here will thank you and some won't look at you, and both of them are right about something."
  > @back "Fair enough. Can I ask something else?" -> hub
